  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Philippines: Conduct and Development of a Feasibility Study for the Governance Structure and other Organizational Development Requirements of the Proposed Philippine National Forensics Authority (PNFA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To conduct a comprehensive feasibility study on the establishment of a Philippine National Forensics Authority. 2) To thoroughly assess the legal, institutional, operational, financial, and technical requirements for its creation. 3) To provide evidence-based recommendations to guide the dedicated Technical Working Group in setting up a sustainable, efficient, and high-standard national facility for forensic services and training.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Government of the Philippines, Department of Foreign Affairs. Indirect beneficiaries: Justice seekers.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to help elevate the standard of investigation of crime in the Philippines by enhancing the forensic capabilities and competence of Philippine law enforcement and justice authorities.</narrative>
  </description>
